<html>
  <head>
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=Cp1252">
    <meta content="Helen" name="generator">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../../javahelp.css" type="text/css">
    <title>Setting probability tables</title>
  </head>
  <body bgcolor="#ffffff">
    <h1>
       <img width="32" height="32" src="../../images/carmenHelpIcons/c2_32.gif" border="0" hspace=
      "0">&nbsp;Setting probability tables
    </h1>
    <hr width="100%" align="left" color="blue" size="2">
    <p>
       One of the most important thing is that you must define the probability of the node when
      depending on its parents.
    </p>
    <p>
       To do it, you must enter in the node properties dialog and then edit the table.
    </p>
    <p>
       &nbsp;
    </p>
    <p>
       Depending of the node type what it is being edited, the table is different as we will show
      now:
    </p>
    <h4>
       Chance node
    </h4>
    <p>
       In a chance node, the table will have the probabilities of each state would take depending
      on the states of the parents or the deterministic value.
    </p>
    <p>
       When the node is created, the table will assign the same value to each state of the node.
    </p>
    <p>
       When the node was already created, and therefore a potential table already exists, if the
      user is adding a new parent, the table is update with 0.0 value.
    </p>
    <p>
       When the node was already created, and therefore a potential table already exists, if the
      user is deleting a node state, the system will distribute the probability value to the other
      states of the node (or if it is a deterministic node and the state that is eliminated is the
      one that have got the value "1", then this value is assigned to the previous state).
    </p>
    <p>
       &nbsp;
    </p>
    <h3>
       Decision node
    </h3>
    <p>
       If the node is a "decision node", then the panel is taken by default "Optimal decision" and
      not having any table.
    </p>
    <p>
       If the user will choice one of the other two types of relation (probabilistic or
      deterministic), then a table will be shown with the same behaviour that in a Chance
      node.&nbsp;
    </p>
    <p>
       &nbsp;
    </p>
    <h3>
       Nodo de utilidad
    </h3>
    <p>
       If a utility node is selected for setting properties, the dialog panel will &nbsp;show nor
      the Type of Relation combobox neither the elements of the chance node. However, a new type of
      relation "Utility" appear and the table will show the the parent states and one single row
      with the values for the utility of the node.
    </p>
    <p>
       This value is not restricted to be between 0 and 1.
    </p>
    <p>
       When the node is created, all these values are set to 0.0.
    </p>
    <p>
       &nbsp;
    </p>
  </body>
</html>
